      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, please have a seat. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Thank you. Well, I suppose what brings me in is... I keep hearing these very clear voices in my apartment. And sometimes when I'm walking through empty museum rooms, too. It sounds like women whispering right from behind the walls, telling me exactly which photographs belong in the archive. It's very specific. \n\nI’ve always had an eye for photography, actually. Back when I was finishing my bachelor's degree, we had to spend hours and hours in the darkroom. The smell of those developing chemicals, it really gets right into your clothes and your hair. I had this lovely wool sweater that smelled like fixer for years. Do you knit? I tried to pick it up last winter because the heating in my building is just dreadful. The radiator clanks all night long. I told the maintenance man about it, but he just looks at me like I'm speaking Greek, and he never wipes his shoes before walking on my rugs...",
