    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "About how long have you been hearing these voices?",
      "targeted_symptom": "psychotic_symptoms_duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, let me think... the voices, and this absolute certainty I have that people are watching my archive—all of that has been present for about eight months now. Yes, eight months. I know that because it started right around the time of that terrible ice storm we had late last winter. \n\nDo you remember that storm? The tree branches outside my building were just coated in it, looking completely encased in glass. I actually tried to photograph them from my living room window, but the glare on the pane was all wrong. I had to open the window to get the shot, and the draft was just freezing! That's when the arthritis really started flaring up again in my knuckles. I ended up buying one of those paraffin wax baths to soak my hands in. Have you ever used one? It feels wonderful, like a warm, heavy glove, but it makes such a terrible mess on the kitchen counter if you aren't careful. I spilled some on a stack of old mail, and it practically sealed my electric bill shut. I had to call the utility company to get my account number, and the woman on the phone had the most grating voice. Not like the whispering women in the walls at all, just very loud and nasal... but yes, about eight months.",
