    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "During these past eight months, have you had times where you felt unusually energized, elated, or on top of the world?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S033",
      "patient_response": "Oh, absolutely. There are days when I wake up and I just feel... radiant. Truly chosen, you know? Like I have this incredible, pulsing energy for my work. I'll put on my good silk blouse—the emerald green one, it really brings out my eyes. I bought it at a lovely little boutique that used to be on 4th street, right next to a bakery that made the most exquisite almond croissants. They closed down years ago, which is such a shame because you just can't find good almond paste anymore. Everything tastes so synthetic now, don't you think? \n\nBut anyway, I get into these moods where I have this grand plan for the photographs, and I'm moving at lightning speed. But then, if someone questions my plan, or tells me I need to slow down, I become absolutely furious. It's as if they are trying to erase me completely! Like my neighbor, Mrs. Gable, she saw me rushing out to the museum with my portfolio recently and had the audacity to tell me to just 'catch my breath.' The nerve! I was so angry. She's always inserting herself where she doesn't belong. Just last week she left a note on my door about my radio being too loud. I was listening to a program about deep-sea diving. Have you ever seen those anglerfish? The ones with the little glowing lanterns on their heads? It's just fascinating how they survive in total darkness down there, carrying their own little light around. I think I'd like to photograph the ocean one day, if I could ever get a waterproof camera.",
