    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "During these past eight months, have you heard the voices at times when your mood and energy felt completely normal?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_3",
      "patient_response": "Yes, actually. There was a stretch of time... oh, I'd say for several weeks... where I wasn't feeling particularly energized or grand at all. Just my usual self, really. But even then, I still heard the women whispering in the apartment. And I remained absolutely convinced that the arts people were monitoring my phone. \n\nSpeaking of my phone, it's one of those older models, a really lovely mustard yellow color. I found it at an estate sale years ago over in the Heights. The woman who owned the house had the most incredible collection of porcelain teacups. Just rows and rows of them, all hand-painted! I bought one with little purple violets on it, but the handle chipped when I was washing it in the sink. I tried to fix it with that super glue, but I ended up getting it all over my fingers. Have you ever glued your fingers together? It is just terrifying! You feel completely trapped. I had to soak my hands in nail polish remover for nearly an hour, and the smell was just atrocious. It gave me such a dreadful headache that I had to lie down with a cold washcloth over my eyes. It's so hard to find a good, soft washcloth these days, isn't it? They all seem to get so scratchy after just a few times in the laundry, no matter how much fabric softener you use...",
